# Themes. bat ships only the dark half of the Visual Studio pair, so the light
# one is the local theme in themes/, registered with `bat cache --build`.
#
# auto:system reads the macOS appearance setting. The default, plain auto,
# instead queries the terminal for its background color, and when that query
# gets no answer -- under `script`, in a pipeline, in a terminal that ignores
# it -- bat drops both themes below and falls back to its compiled-in Monokai
# Extended, whose off-white foreground is unreadable on a light background.
# Ghostty follows the system appearance too, so the two always agree.
--theme=auto:system
--theme-light="Visual Studio Light+"
--theme-dark="Visual Studio Dark+"
